# tally 2.2.1 P30 (L §4.4 l.667 to l.671): an operation decides over an interval only what holds for every value
# the interval can hold; its ends stand for them only where it is monotone and gives a value everywhere between.
# B2: day_of(mm, days_between(d1, w) / 2) refuses on 03-10 and 03-12 (4.5, 5.5) and gives 2026-02-05 on 03-11,
# so the hole. tally 2.2 printed the low end's refusal, RUN-NOT-INT 4.5.
=== b2_dayof.tally
model b2
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
input w: date
input wl: date
input d0: date
input d1: date
input de: date
input n2: num
input n100: num
input m1: num
input mm: month
version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = window(2026-03-10, 2026-03-12) "c"
  wl = window(2026-01-01, 2027-06-01) "c"
  d0 = 2026-03-11 "c"
  d1 = 2026-03-01 "c"
  de = 2025-12-30 "c"
  n2 = 2 "c"
  n100 = 100 "c"
  m1 = -1 "c"
  mm = 2026-02 "c"
ask dofh: day_of(mm, days_between(d1, w) / n2)
ask dofh_a: day_of(mm, days_between(d1, w) / n2) with w = 2026-03-10
ask dofh_b: day_of(mm, days_between(d1, w) / n2) with w = 2026-03-11
ask dofh_c: day_of(mm, days_between(d1, w) / n2) with w = 2026-03-12
=== expect
dofh: ?"date within window(2026-03-10, 2026-03-12) not precise enough for day_of" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
dofh_a: refused: RUN-NOT-INT 4.5 is not an integer
  pinned: w = 2026-03-10
  cut 2026-01-01
dofh_b: 2026-02-05
  pinned: w = 2026-03-11
  cut 2026-01-01
dofh_c: refused: RUN-NOT-INT 5.5 is not an integer
  pinned: w = 2026-03-12
  cut 2026-01-01
warning: WARN-UNREAD input d0 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input de is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input m1 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input n100 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input wl is read by nothing
